Whitney Hodges: opening the emails. Um, so I think by removing that, and then by changing up the subject line to the initial email, that that's going to help. I also think, just like in some of these text message alternatives, just making sure that people are aware that you have emailed them, right, and almost kind of, like, pointing them to the inbox.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.000
Scott & Krista: Right.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:45.000
Whitney Hodges: I think that that's going to help also. I totally hear you. I don't think that we need to be asking them to schedule a tour right away in the in the text message, if that's not really kind of what matches with their with their customer journey.

