00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
Scott & Krista: drip campaign.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Yeah. I don't know off the top of my head if it's already included. If it's not included, I do want to include it because I do think that that is useful for sure.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.000
Scott & Krista: All right.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:59.000
Whitney Hodges: What I really want to see more of at this point, right, is the…

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:19.000
Whitney Hodges: those initial touch points encouraging responses from these leads, right? And so, you know, right now with the current text message, it kind of like puts the ball in your court of like, okay, I'm going to reach out to you shortly, right? And it sounds like maybe that's something that Valerie is doing.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:36.000
Whitney Hodges: But I do think that ending the text message with some sort of question that they need to answer, and it doesn't have to be them scheduling a private tour, but something that's trying to get a response from them, I think, is going to be helpful. So, I mean, it could be as simple as, you know, do you have, um…

